/-!
# The Held group in its ATLAS degree-2058 construction

`Held.He` is the subgroup generated by the explicit permutations from
ATLAS representation `HeG1-p2058B0`, with inherited `Group` and `Finite`
instances. It is available as the target of multiplicative equivalences.
The construction is certified by kernel-checked inverse tables, exact orders
2, 7, and 17 of the standard generators and their product, and all seven
relators in John Bray's ATLAS presentation `HeG1-P1`. The canonical map
from that presentation onto `Held.He` is proved surjective. The generating
pair also proves that `Held.He` is perfect and not solvable.

Sources:
* https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/HeG1-p2058B0
* https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/pres/HeG1-P1

The original source files, action-convention conversion, and reproduction
instructions are retained in `Model/Source/`. Neither classification nor
an order-based recognition assumption is used. The exact group order and
simplicity are not claimed by this construction module.
-/
